    "result": "Done! The frai-core test suite now passes completely. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n### 1. **Governance module export** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\nThe test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. Added named exports for:\n- `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n- `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`\n- `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`\n- `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n### 2. **Toxicity metric signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\nThe `DEFAULT_METRICS` array was calling all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` has a different signature: `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. When called with references as the second argument, it was incorrectly using the references array as banned terms instead of using default banned terms. I wrapped the metric call to only pass outputs: `(outputs, references) => toxicityMetric(outputs)`.\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests passing across 8 test files, and all public exports remain intact.",
